From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NotAlexNoyle <alexnoyle@icloud.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Nov 2025 15:27:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Keep chunks loaded during villager curing

Holds a per-entity chunk ticket (radius 2, entity-ticking at the center)
while a zombie villager is converting, so the cure finishes even if the
player who started it leaves or the server restarts mid-cure.

The ticket is added when the conversion starts (player, API, or NBT
replay on chunk load), re-homed when the entity crosses a chunk border,
and refreshed every tick the entity ticks. It expires 20 seconds after
the last refresh, which bounds every removal path that bypasses
remove() (portal trips, cross-world /tp, UNLOADED_WITH_PLAYER, chunk
unload, duplicate-UUID regen). Known paths release it immediately.

Zombie villagers saved mid-cure by earlier builds of this patch, which
disabled AI and used /forceload, get their AI back and their chunk
un-forced on load.

